@end iftex
@caption{@strong{Figure 2.13:} Recursive plans for @code{right-split} and @code{corner-split}.}
@end float

@noindent
We can produce balanced patterns by branching upwards as well as towards the
right (see @ref{Exercise 2.44}, @ref{Figure 2.13} and @ref{Figure 2.14}):

@lisp
(define (corner-split painter n)
  (if (= n 0)
      painter
      (let ((up (up-split painter (- n 1)))
            (right (right-split painter 
                                (- n 1))))
        (let ((top-left (beside up up))
              (bottom-right (below right 
                                   right))
              (corner (corner-split painter 
                                    (- n 1))))
          (beside (below painter top-left)
                  (below bottom-right 
                         corner))))))
@end lisp

@float
@anchor{Figure 2.14}
@ifinfo
@quotation
